    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PAINTED BY J. P. BUTTERWORTH\nDonald Mo Kany Org. Builder of the Leviathon\nCLIPPER SUP «GREAT REPUBLIC\"\nLITH. BY N. CURRIER",
      "THE\nPRESiDENT\nSPECiAL\nSherry Dubonnet Campari Dry Vamouth Sake\nManhattan Martini\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Voila Collins\nScotch Bourbon Canadian\nGin Vodka\nOUR SELECTiON OF VINTAGE WiNES\nGreat Wines of Burgundy Great Wines of Bordeau\nChampagne\nContreau Drambuie Benedictine\nCremo do Mentho Cognac VSOP Birticine and Brandy\nMENU\nNot au Vent de Ville Royale\nCHICKEN ROYALE IN PATTY SHELL\nOR\nNot au lánt de Crabe Naplun\nCRAB NEPTUNE IN PATTY SHELL\nMacedoine de Truits\nMACEDOINE OF FRESH FRUIT\nDemi-Tasse\nDEMITASSE\nCafé Americain\nAMERICAN COFFEE\nThe Orange Pekoe\nORANGE PEKOE TEA\nPAN AMERiCAN CUiSiNE BY MAXiM'S DE PARiS",
      "Built by Donald McKay and launched in 1853 in East Boston, the clipper ship\n\"Great Republic\"\nwas the summit of achievement in the world of sailing ships.\nShe was, from the standpoint of size, appearance and cost... the King of Clippers.\nThe\n\"Great Republic\"\nwas considered the largest,\nsharpest and most magnif-\nicent craft ever produced by any nation or age. Before\nshe had barely tasted\nwas a network of flames. She was later rebuilt but with her tonnage,\nsail plan and spars reduced.\nLike Pan Am's modern Clippers® of the air, the early clipper ships traveled the\nlanes of commerce to all far places of the world. Pan Am's Clipper fleet of the\nCentury\ncommercial\ndeveloped.\nClippers that helped Pan Am establish an unparalleled record for safety, speed\nand service.\nThis is a faithful reproduction of an authentic Currier \u0026 Ives lithograph,\nrepro-\nduced through the courtesy of the Mariners Museum, Newport News,\nVirginia.\nITHO U.S. A\n011.130.00-"
    ],
